From 093a1e398e5fd0b28d107227f3634cd2495b76d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dinadur <59811564+dinadur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:04:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] B70: shadow groundedness judges citation-list answers;
 cleaner claims

- Answers that cite only in a trailing 'Citations:'/'Sources:' line or section
  had no inline-linked sentences and produced zero shadow claims. Substantive
  uncited sentences (>= 40 chars, not table rows) are now judged against the
  best-matching windows across every listed page (mode=list in the log).
- Sentence splitting handles a bold close after the full stop ('...ally.** It').
- Empty '()' left where a link sat in parentheses is removed from claim text.
- All excerpts for one claim share a 1400-char budget: Clef's server batch is
  1024 tokens and three 800-char windows of dense spec text overflowed it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 agent/product_groundedness.py            | 112 ++++++++++++++++++-----
 tests/agent/test_product_groundedness.py |  78 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 165 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

